{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 office-wide internet outage. Reporter: Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, America/New_York). Reported: the whole office floor lost internet and nobody can work. Checks: the account is active with no blocks and VPN access is on. Laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:22:08Z. It may have checked in before the outage started, or over a hotspot or another path; not confirmed. Floor printer BL-PR-FL2 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-09T09:28:08Z, no warnings. That printer status may or may not be linked to this outage. Per KB-014, an office network down for several people is P1 and must be escalated. Tier 1 can't fix this from the user side. Still needed: check the office WAN/ISP circuit, edge firewall/router, core switch and DHCP/DNS for the site; confirm which floors or sites are affected; open an ISP ticket if the circuit is down; send updates to the reporter.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this. An outage across the whole office has to go to our network team, so I've escalated it as top priority (P1) and they're looking into it now. You don't need to do anything on individual laptops. Restarting them won't help if the office connection itself is down. Until it's back, anyone who has to work can use a phone hotspot and connect to the VPN. The network team will keep you updated. If you know whether other floors are affected, or when the outage started, please reply with that so we can narrow it down faster.",
  "internal_note": "P1, office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Account active, no blocks, VPN access on. Laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:22:08Z. It may have checked in before the outage or over another path; not confirmed. Floor printer BL-PR-FL2 shows offline since 2026-10-09T09:28:08Z with no warnings; not confirmed that this is related. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) per KB-014 and P1 policy. Still needed: check the site WAN/ISP circuit, edge firewall/router, core switch and DHCP/DNS; confirm which floors or sites are affected.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
